,"findings":"I found no major defects. The new tests pass when run on their own (8 of 8, with `--test-name-pattern`), and I tried the edge cases below in the clone. There are two minor issues.\n\n**1. Piped evidence is refused, though the error suggests only odd files are** (minor, **verified**)\n- Where: `src/evidence.ts:44`\n- Scenario: `git gud review wip --stage honesty --evidence <(git gloss lint wip)` stops with `error: --evidence /dev/fd/63: is not a regular file`. So does `echo ok | git gud review ... --evidence /dev/stdin`.\n- Why it matters: the change wants you to hand over output you already have, and process substitution or a pipe is the obvious way to do that. The README lists what is refused (directories, NUL bytes, size limits) but not pipes, so this is a surprise. It is also inconsistent: `/dev/zero`, a character device, is accepted and read.\n- Fix: since the read is already bounded and non-blocking, read FIFOs normally, or say in the README and the error that pipes are not accepted.\n\n**2. For branch reviews, the honesty instructions rule out an ISSUES verdict for \"Across the branch\" findings** (minor, **read**)\n- Where: `src/stages.ts:120`\n- Scenario: on a range target, git-gloss's honesty prompt adds item 6, \"Across the branch\": later commits that undo earlier ones, unglossed commits, and so on. The new text says to \"give VERDICT: ISSUES only for mismatches or missing risks you found\".\n- Outcome: a branch where a later commit reverts an earlier one, or where commits are unglossed, gets `VERDICT: CLEAN`, and that verdict is recorded with the review. Before this change, git-gloss's own verdict line counted those findings.\n- The same wording also stops item 4 (Simplifications) from producing ISSUES. That may be intended, but the text only explains that items 2 and 3 are skipped.\n\n**Things I checked that hold up:**\n- **Rules and evidence placement:** they are always inserted before the first separator. In git-gloss's prompt, nothing the author controls comes before that separator (I checked `review.js`), so a forged separator in the diff, the commit message or a file name can't move them.\n- **Fencing:** hostile backtick runs and a fake `# Material under review` heading stay inside the evidence block.\n- **Escapes and controls:** escape sequences, C1 controls and bidi characters are stripped, from file names and error paths too.\n- **Bounded reads:** `/dev/zero` is refused without hanging, and a file of exactly 128 KiB is accepted.\n- **Ordering:** bad evidence stops the run before any reviewer starts.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
