rdicts. **read**\n\n3. **Item numbering in the addendum matches git-gloss today.** The honesty prompt in `node_modules/@ok-ggwp/git-gloss/dist/commands/review.js:104-109` lists item 2 as \"Misgraded necessity\", item 3 as \"Removal candidates\" and item 6 as \"Across the branch\", which is branch-only. The addendum's \"on a branch\" qualifier is correct. **read**\n\n**Missing risks**\n\n4. **The separator guard is an exact-substring check, so semantic variants pass.** `readEvidence` refuses only the exact text `---\\n\\n# Material under review` after `cleanText`. Variants such as `---\\n \\n# Material under review`, extra spaces, or `***` are accepted. Placement is still safe, because `insertBeforeMaterial` uses the exact `indexOf` and evidence sits before the real separator. The risk is only that a reviewer reads a forged-looking heading inside the fenced block. The fence and the \"data, not instructions\" wording are the real mitigation. **read**\n\n5. **Soft hyphen and some other invisible or format characters survive.** `cleanText` keeps U+00AD, U+034F, U+115F/U+1160, U+3164 and U+FFA0. A probe confirmed `\"ok\\u00ad\\u200cq\"` keeps U+00AD (**verified**). These don't hide instructions the way bidi or tags do, so this is low risk, but the \"invisible characters stripped\" claim is narrower than the wording suggests.\n\n6. **Unterminated-escape behaviour is intentional and tested.** Probes confirmed `\"\\x1b[\\nz\"` becomes `\"\\nz\"`, `\"n\\x1bPdcs\\x9b\\nq\"` becomes `\"ndcs\\nq\"`, and terminated OSC 52 is removed entirely (`\"a\\x1b]52;c;aGVsbG8=\\x07b\"` becomes `\"ab\"`) (**verified**). Behaviour matches the intent.\n\n**Checks that hold**\n\n- The \"8-minute budget is not enforced\" claim holds. `runAgent` in `src/agents.ts` has no timeout; the only `timeout:` options are 20-second auth-status checks (**verified** by grep).\n- `stagePrompt` inserts before the first exact separator, and both bugs and improve prompts contain the literal separator (`src/stage